| `firmware/App/driver/voice.h` | verbatim | the voice-prompt interface `audio.c` includes (voice prompts are off for the RA89R, so nothing calls it) |
| `firmware/App/app/app.h` | adapted | one port addition: `CheckKeys()` is declared there, because `app/app.c` defines it but the K1 header does not |
| `firmware/App/driver/bk4819.c` | adapted (port addition) | `BK4819_ToggleGpioOut` mirrors the two status-LED outputs (`GPIO5_PIN1_RED`, `GPIO6_PIN2_GREEN`) onto this board's MCU LED (`driver/led.c`, PA13/PA14); the chip register write is unchanged |
| `firmware/App/app/main.c` | adapted | one port change in `MAIN_Key_EXIT`: a short EXIT press with nothing to cancel (no digits typed, not scanning) calls `COMMON_SwitchVFOs()`, because this radio has no dedicated A/B key -- it is the K1's F + 2 action |
| `firmware/App/ui/battery.c`, `ui/scanner.c`, `ui/status.c`, `ui/welcome.c`, `ui/status.h`, `driver/py25q16.h` | verbatim | the status line (`UI_DisplayStatus`, including its battery drawing), the boot/welcome screen and the external SPI NOR flash interface the welcome screen reads its boot messages from |
